--- /dev/null
+++ b/SMS-INTEGRATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+The page runs in an explicitly labeled local demo by default. No SMS is sent; the demo code is 123456 and expires after five minutes.
+
+To connect real SMS delivery, define `window.DAILY_GRIND_VERIFICATION_API = '/api/phone-verification'` in a script before `verification.js` loads. Implement these same-origin JSON endpoints:
+
+- `POST /api/phone-verification/send` receives `{ phone }` in international format and returns `{ challengeId }`. Calling it again requests a replacement code.
+- `POST /api/phone-verification/verify` receives `{ challengeId, code }` and returns `{ verified: true }` only after server verification. Errors should use an appropriate non-2xx status and `{ message }`.
+
+The backend must bind challenges to the current session and phone, securely generate and store short-lived codes, invalidate used and replaced codes, enforce resend and attempt limits, and protect requests against CSRF. Never accept the demo code in production. The server is the authority on expiry and verification; client controls provide feedback only.
+
+Send human-readable SMS text followed by a final line formatted exactly as `@your-domain.example #123456`, substituting the deployed hostname (without scheme, port, or path) and generated code. Serve over HTTPS. WebOTP starts before dispatch and aborts on manual submission, resend, editing the phone, or page exit. Unsupported browsers retain system one-time-code autofill and manual entry.
